    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0086" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.00/2–1047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate at Hanoi</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-14T17:00:00-05:00">February 14,
                            1947—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. Urtel 51 Feb. 10.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d84-f1"/> Re Vietnam report that
                    Secy’s declaration showed that international opinion does not wish see war in
                    Vietnam, Secy in Feb 7 press conf said for attribution but not quotation “We are
                    naturally deeply interested troubled situation Indochina and naturally are
                    hopeful they can find pacific basis for its adjustment”.</p>
                <p>Sent Hanoi 15. Repeated Saigon 32.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
